{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "scenario_id": "float64_to_int64_fractional",
  "title": "float64 to int64 with fractional values",
  "category": "numeric",
  "description": "A float64 column becomes int64. v0 holds fractional values; each v1 value is the v0 value truncated toward zero. The values distinguish truncation from rounding: 1.5 -> 1, 2.999 -> 2, -1.5 -> -1.",
  "notes": [
    "Truncation is what this producer did. It is not a statement of how a cast ought to behave; rounding, rejection and nulling are all observed in practice.",
    "NaN and infinities are deliberately absent: they have no int64 value, and including them would mix a second change into this scenario."
  ],
  "tags": [
    "change-type",
    "floating-point",
    "integer",
    "narrowing",
    "precision-loss"
  ],
